P2. --exec-bin DIR.

/bin/x and /usr/bin/x become DIR/x when that file exists, for the program
proot starts, every program a tracee executes, and the interpreter of a
script. Nothing is bound over /bin or /usr/bin, so a program keeps the path
it was run from. The option has no effect when the guest rootfs is not /.

